      "review_notes": "Independent Poisson additivity handles unit-rate draws; independent binomial thinning handles the final fractional rate. The single expectation theorem identifies both cases with canonical Mathlib Poisson(x/y). The remaining-rate loop is straightforward strong induction. Tests explicitly establish real rate(1,2)=1/2, rate(6,2)=3 and zero rate, check thinning endpoints p=0 and p=1 plus the fractional case, infinite continuation values and arbitrary resource framing."
