      "review_notes": "The enclosing width is the least power of two covering the target interval. A private binary-word loop reuses the reviewed RandomBits prefix expectation. Accepted words preserve exactly the canonical uniform target credit; at most half the enclosing words are rejected, funding retry amplification by two. The obvious CTE retry loop follows this inequality. Tests cover widths1/4/5, the exact no-rejection kernel at power-of-two width4, infinite off-support credit at width1 and arbitrary framed callers. The candidate helper remains private in the same file, keeping its elementary component proof next to its use."
